          "@id": "edam:topic_2269"
        }
      ],
      "sc:author": "Srdjan Sarikas",
      "sc:description": "synfit fits 4- and 5-parameter Hill curves to dose-response data and reports IC50/EC50 with 95% confidence intervals. For two-drug combination matrices it fits both drugs jointly and reports Bliss independence, Loewe additivity, HSA and ZIP synergy side by side. Free, runs in the browser, no install. Single-drug fits use explicit noise models (lognormal, heteroscedastic Gaussian) and give 95% confidence intervals on every parameter; inverse prediction returns a concentration with its confidence interval from a given response. Plots can be exported as PNG/SVG, outliers excluded, and read-only share links created. The numerical core is the open-source Python package synfit (MIT).",
      "sc:featureList": [
        {
          "@id": "edam:operation_3659"
        },
        {
          "@id": "edam:operation_2238"
        }
      ],
